{"total_count":21,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/events","html_url":"https://github.com/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407","id":2442495188,"node_id":"I_kwDOAzkJ986RlYTU","number":407,"title":"Update the benchmark suite and bring it into the CI runner [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7277527310,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAzkJ988AAAABscZBDg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"D7B4F0","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7277528655,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAzkJ988AAAABscZGTw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"FABF75","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2024-08-01T13:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:45:24Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Update the benchmark suite and bring it into the CI runner [$400]\r\n\r\nQuantumOptics.jl has an in-depth benchmarking suite that has bitrotted in the last few years. To claim this bounty:\r\n\r\n- Set up a benchmark-on-CI infrastructure (e.g. similar to the one in QuantumClifford.jl) that runs QuantumOptics-specific benchmarks on each pull request\r\n- Include all old benchmarks in that infrastructure (reusing the existing benchmark suite as much as possible) and make it easy to add new micro-benchmarks as new features get developed.\r\n\r\nThe above are for the sake of the developers of this package. However, this bounty also requires the following to be done for the sake of users:\r\n\r\n- Fix up the capability to run benchmarks in comparison to popular python packages (qutip) and add comparative Julia packages (QuantumToolbox.jl)\r\n- Create a makefile that let's a developer to easily update the webpage presenting these comparative benchmarks to the user.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Understanding of Julia's and Python's benchmarking infrastructure.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov and/or @david-pl \r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132","id":2399058498,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6O_rpC","number":132,"title":"Improve Makie visualization capabilities [$200]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183765670,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-Qpg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:200","name":"bounty:200","color":"8F21A4","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":22,"created_at":"2024-07-09T19:48:27Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T02:58:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Project: Improve Makie visualization capabilities [$200]\r\n\r\nWe use Makie for visualizing the state of a simulated network. We can visualize the state of registers, the content of these registers, some tag information, etc. There is much more information that can be tracked visually though. This project is about fleshing out these visualization features.\r\n[This list of issues can be a useful guide to features that need to be implemented](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3Avisualization), but you should feel free to suggest deviations from these guidelines if you have different ideas -- however the scope of the project should be set at the start of the project, e.g. by discussing it in this thread.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Understanding of the Makie plotting library\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 1 month\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/132/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131","id":2398792222,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6O-qoe","number":131,"title":"More thorough benchmarks [$200]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4234256537,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc78YaCZ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183765670,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-Qpg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:200","name":"bounty:200","color":"8F21A4","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":25,"created_at":"2024-07-09T17:40:31Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T02:55:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n\n# Project: \"More thorough benchmarks\" [$200]\n\nWe have a small benchmark suite already implemented, which is executed as part of our CI runs. It is defined in the `benchmark` folder and reported for each pull request. **We would like to expand this benchmark suite** to include many more facets of this library. E.g. basic register operations using a variety of backends; queries and tags and locks on registers and channels; time to import; time to run examples. The new benchmarks should be legible, easy to follow, and organized by topic. Most of them should be microbenchmarks testing only one concept, but a few holistic benchmarks would make sense as well.\n\n**Required skills**: Generic Julia skills.\n\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\n\n**Duration**: 1 month\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/131/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67","id":2399158316,"node_id":"I_kwDOIf3lgs6PAEAs","number":67,"title":"All struct fields should be (concretely) typed (potentially with a type parameter) [$200]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7179653769,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIf3lgs8AAAABq_DSiQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue"},{"id":7184070727,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIf3lgs8AAAABrDQ4Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/labels/bounty:200","name":"bounty:200","color":"7A01C7","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2024-07-09T20:28:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T20:40:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Project: All struct fields should be (concretely) typed (potentially with a type parameter) [$200]\r\n\r\nMany of the symbolic types in this library are rather clumsily defined, without much attention being paid to the types of their fields. The goal of this bounty is to specify them and parameterize them as much as possible and reasonable, in preparation for next steps like the use of sum types and Unityper.jl. [This forum discussion might provide useful background](https://discourse.julialang.org/t/when-is-it-better-to-use-non-concrete-types-in-structs/29041/11).\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Understanding of Symbolics.jl and Julia's type system\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 1 month\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/67/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99","id":2442860730,"node_id":"I_kwDOBfanzM6Rmxi6","number":99,"title":"Use JuliaLowering.jl for a cleaner way to transform resumable functions to finite state machines [$600]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7278164896,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBfanzM8AAAABsc_7oA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"430B33","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7781357533,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBfanzM8AAAABz84X3Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/labels/bounty:600","name":"bounty:600","color":"734E67","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2024-08-01T16:17:28Z","updated_at":"2026-06-13T22:19:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Edit: #100 has fixed most of these issues without relying on the not-yet-published JuliaLowering.jl. It uses a local reimplementation of most scoping rules of the language, thus missing edge cases might exist. Leaving this (now smaller) bounty for future work of moving this implementation to JuliaLowering, to provide a more centralized source-of-truth on scoping.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis software transform annotated julia functions into finite state machines that can be paused and re-entered. The issue tracker has many reports of edge cases related to unsupported syntax or bugs due to loss of scope information. PR #92 even attempts to fix some of these issues, but it is too limited and ad-hoc.\r\n\r\nJuliaLowering.jl is itself only experimental these days, but it should have enough capabilities for solving most of the issues depicted here.\r\n\r\nTo claim this bounty, \"simply\" fix all these issues ;) (or fix many or the related issues)\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Deep understanding of Julia macros, syntax, and lowering.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 3 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaDynamics/ResumableFunctions.jl/issues/99/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64","id":3173631773,"node_id":"I_kwDOOstdXs69Kccd","number":64,"title":"Leadership Task: Research Sustainable Funding Models for ONM","user":{"login":"DRosen766","id":96319586,"node_id":"U_kgDOBb24Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96319586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766","html_url":"https://github.com/DRosen766","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DRosen766/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"neural-loop","id":654993,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDk5Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/654993?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop","html_url":"https://github.com/neural-loop","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neural-loop/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"aMarcireau","id":5418893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTg4OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5418893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau","html_url":"https://github.com/aMarcireau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"beffiong1","id":135363557,"node_id":"U_kgDOCBF75Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135363557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1","html_url":"https://github.com/beffiong1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beffiong1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-06-25T00:02:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T18:47:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"aMarcireau","id":5418893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTg4OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5418893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau","html_url":"https://github.com/aMarcireau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aMarcireau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":1},"body":"## 🧠 Open Neuromorphic Leadership Task\n\n### Context & Objectives\nOpen Neuromorphic currently operates on a volunteer basis. To ensure long-term sustainability and support growth (e.g., covering website hosting costs, offering prizes for challenges), we need to establish a lightweight and transparent funding mechanism.\n\n**Objectives:**\n- Investigate fiscal sponsorship options (e.g., NumFOCUS, Software Freedom Conservancy, Open Collective) to allow ONM to accept donations and sponsorships while aligning with our open-source, community-driven ethos.\n- Draft a basic operational budget estimating annual costs for infrastructure (domain/hosting, CI/CD, event platforms).\n- Outline a simple sponsorship prospectus, including potential sponsorship tiers for ONM initiatives (e.g., Hardware Guide, Grand Challenge).\n\n**Deliverable:**\nA summary report presented to the ONM community outlining the pros and cons of 1-2 recommended sustainable funding options.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-neuromorphic/communications/issues/64/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138","id":2441273974,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6RguJ2","number":138,"title":"Implement a new interactive example [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183794196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrDAAFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"86C87A","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2024-08-01T02:06:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T13:35:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Implement a new interactive example [$400]\r\n\r\nWe have a growing collection of interactive examples in this repository, showcasing a variety of interesting networking setups and their dynamics. To claim this bounty propose, discuss, and implement new examples of a networking simulations of interest to you. Multiple people can claim this bounty repeatedly with different projects.\r\n\r\nSubmissions will have to be well documented and tested, in a format that makes them as easy to run as the already existing examples.\r\n\r\nSome examples can be seen running online at https://areweentangledyet.com/\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Knowledge of the phenomenon or protocol being simulated in the example, comfort with visualization libraries like Makie.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137","id":2441265567,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6RgsGf","number":137,"title":"Implement a networking protocol primitive [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183794196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrDAAFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"86C87A","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2024-08-01T01:58:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T12:57:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Implement a networking protocol primitive [$400]\r\n\r\nThere are many interesting protocols and networking primitives yet to be added to this library. To claim this bounty propose and then implement a protocol for the ProtocolZoo submodule. Multiple people can claim this bounty (repeatedly) for new implementations. For substantial development efforts bigger bounties can be approved.\r\n\r\nTests and documentation have to be part of such submissions.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Deep knowledge of the protocol being implemented and rough understanding of networking simulations with this library.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n**Publication**: In the next 2 years we plan to release a paper in a selective journal about this software. Contributing to this issue would deserve a co-authorship status on such a paper (if the contributor so desires)\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73","id":2442762701,"node_id":"I_kwDOIf3lgs6RmZnN","number":73,"title":"A backend for QuantumCumulants.jl [$200]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7179653769,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIf3lgs8AAAABq_DSiQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue"},{"id":7184070727,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIf3lgs8AAAABrDQ4Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/labels/bounty:200","name":"bounty:200","color":"7A01C7","default":false,"description":""},{"id":7620071857,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIf3lgs8AAAABxjERsQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/labels/bounty:reserved","name":"bounty:reserved","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2024-08-01T15:27:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T20:27:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A backend for QuantumCumulants.jl [$200]\r\n\r\nThe QuantumCumulants library (part of the QuantumOptics organization) provides for an elegant way to solve truncated differential equations for expectation values of quantum observables. To claim this bounty you need to create an `express` interface for converting symbolic objects from QuantumSymbolics into objects QuantumCumulants can work with.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Knowledge of the QuantumCumulants library\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov and/or @david-pl\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/73/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449","id":3261051663,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CX7MP","number":449,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for networkx [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"Syuizen","id":15939422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTM5NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15939422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen","html_url":"https://github.com/Syuizen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":33,"created_at":"2025-07-24T19:45:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T12:22:37Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Syuizen","id":15939422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTM5NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15939422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen","html_url":"https://github.com/Syuizen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `networkx` wrapper [$400]\n\nUsing networkx through PythonCall.jl is trivially easy. This bounty is mostly about creating a new NetworkX.jl wrapper (by using PythonCall.jl) that provides quality-of-life improvements, \n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the networkx structures\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the newly created networkx wrapper types (so that networkx types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to networkx implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in NetworkX `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::NXAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the networkx implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to networkx graphs if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in networkx that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that NetworkX is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the PythonCall package\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447","id":3260998830,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CXuSu","number":447,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C++ library `LEMON` [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9028522432,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGiRRwA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:reserved","name":"bounty:reserved","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"AJ0070","id":87864439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODY0NDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87864439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070","html_url":"https://github.com/AJ0070","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":20,"created_at":"2025-07-24T19:27:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T23:47:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"AJ0070","id":87864439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODY0NDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87864439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070","html_url":"https://github.com/AJ0070","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `LEMON` wrapper [$400]\n\nThe JuliaGraphs/LEMONGraphs.jl package already exists and provides an extremely barebones wrapper for the LEMON C++ library. It is barely more than a proof of concept for the build infrastructure. A lot of this work probably will not be directly in the Graphs.jl repository.\n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the C++ structures of LEMON (slow converters already exist for simple graphs)\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the LEMONGraph types (so that LEMONGraph types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to LEMON implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in LEMONGraphs `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::LEMONAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the C++ implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to LEMONGraph if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in LEMON that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that LEMONGraphs is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the CxxWrap interface package.\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vega/vega/issues/4221","id":3874887023,"node_id":"I_kwDOAHn8vM7m9hVv","number":4221,"title":"Bug & Feature Bounty","user":{"login":"PBI-David","id":86846675,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2ODQ2Njc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86846675?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David","html_url":"https://github.com/PBI-David","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PBI-David/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":923852183,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5MjM4NTIxODM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/labels/help-wanted","name":"help-wanted","color":"d8c243","default":false,"description":"For potential community contributions"},{"id":8029597012,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAHn8vM8AAAAB3pntVA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/labels/developer-experience","name":"developer-experience","color":"8AEDB7","default":false,"description":"For changes related to the development of Vega itself"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2026-01-30T09:41:45Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T08:04:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"@domoritz please feel free to close if this is not the appropriate place for this discussion. \n\nI wondered if it was possible to start a bug bounty? Vega and Vega-Lite are used extensively and sometimes users encounter frustrating bugs or need features which the maintainers don't have the bandwidth to implement as everyone is donating their time. Would it be possible for people to offer payment to fix certain bugs or implement specific features? \n\nIf there is no official way to do this via the Vega and Vega-Lite ecosystem due to complexities of payments etc, would it be possible to have a sticky _Issue_ where users can post bugs they want fixed or features implemented and then interested developers could respond and they could take the conversation offline. Anything fixed or implemented would then get fed back into the Vega and Vega-Lite codebase so the wider community would also benefit.\n\nThoughts welcome. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vega/vega/issues/4221/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446","id":3260869845,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CXOzV","number":446,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C library `igraphs` [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2025-07-24T18:45:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-29T02:45:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `igraphs` wrapper [$400]\n\nThe JuliaGraphs/IGraphs.jl package already exists and provides a simple low-level wrapper for the igraph C library. A lot of this work probably will not be directly in the Graphs.jl repository.\n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the C structures of igraph (slow converters already exist for simple graphs and some vectors/matrices)\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the IGraph types (so that IGraph types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to igraph implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in IGraphs `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::IGraphAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the C implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to IGraph if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in igraph that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that IGraphs is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty.\n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the Julia-C interface\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/446/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448","id":3261019026,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CXzOS","number":448,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C library `very_nauty` [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2025-07-24T19:34:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T16:57:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `very_nauty` wrapper [$400]\n\nThe JuliaGraphs/VNGraphs.jl package already exists and provides a simple low-level wrapper for the C library. A lot of this work probably will not be directly in the Graphs.jl repository.\n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the C structures of very_nauty (slow converters already exist for simple graphs)\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the VNGraph types (so that VNGraph types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to very_nauty implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in VNGraphs `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::VNAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the C implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to VNGraph if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in very_nauty that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that VNGraphs is necessary. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the Julia-C interface\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/448/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129","id":2398752899,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6O-hCD","number":129,"title":"Tensor Networks Backend [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183794196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrDAAFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"86C87A","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2024-07-09T17:16:05Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T06:37:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Project: \"Tensor Networks Backend\" [$400]\r\n\r\nThis project depends on first completing https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSymbolics.jl/issues/63\r\n\r\nThis simulation library can easily work with state vectors and stabilizer tableaux, thanks to the existence of QuantumSymbolics backends for them. **To complete this project the contributor will need to plug in a tensor network backend, so that simulations can be performed using tensor network numerical representations.** Some of the currently existing examples already perform simulations using both stabilizer states and state vectors. These examples will need to be updated to include tensor network simulations as well. A new example of a simulation that would be too expensive to run without tensor networks would be necessary as part of this contribution, in order to showcase and document the new functionality.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Familiarity with tensor networks and with the QuantumSymbolics package.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: Can be reserved for 2 months and potentially extended.\r\n\r\n**Publication**: In the next 2 years we plan to release a paper in a selective journal about this software. Contributing to this issue would deserve a co-authorship status on such a paper (if the contributor so desires)\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/129/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/security/issues/113","id":3193189065,"node_id":"I_kwDOF1BASc6-VDLJ","number":113,"title":"[Brainstorming] Security funding ideas and priorities","user":{"login":"krassowski","id":5832902,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MzI5MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5832902?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski","html_url":"https://github.com/krassowski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-07-01T16:57:23Z","updated_at":"2025-08-19T17:18:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Trying to understand how security group could benefit from potential funding, during the meeting today we discussed some ideas on how we could improve Jupyter security and reduce backlog of unresolved vulnerability reports. The four areas that we bounced off were:\n\n- tools which increase productivity of security managers e.g.\n  - snyk (I will let others elaborate)\n  - sandboxes with various OSes for remediation developers (e.g. to test patches for issues specific to Windows or Mac)\n- bug bounty or other way to encourage submissions, especially if submissions come already with mitigation/patch proposal\n  - we discussed that bug bounty programmes are expensive and generate a lot of work (triage/coordination/remediation) so might be more suitable to pursue in future years\n  - we noted that some platforms allow to contribute a small amount of money to existing bug bounty wrapper programmes\n  - we noted that some high profile organisations and corporations do not offer monetary rewards at all, and instead encourage submissions by publicising the contribution (social media, entry on a public, branded website as a badge of honour - on top of standard GitHub credits); this could be well suited for Jupyter and require mostly time of a coordinator (rather than a developer) who would take care of it\n- security retreat/working meeting\n- dispersing some funds for remediation of existing vulnerability reports (as previously discussed in around never realised plan to use funds from Tidelift to do that) - with its all benefits and potential drawbacks [as discussed previously](https://github.com/jupyter-governance/ec-team-compass/issues/20#issuecomment-2726562745)\n\nI'm opening the issue for transparency, to highlight that I am looking into what proposals could be submitted for consideration (whether for Jupyter Foundation or for Tidelift fund - if that ever comes to fruition), and to gather more ideas.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyter/security/issues/113/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808/events","html_url":"https://github.com/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808","id":549191872,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDkxOTE4NzI=","number":2808,"title":"Host admin can export contributor data CSV","user":{"login":"alanna","id":5498878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0OTg4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5498878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna","html_url":"https://github.com/alanna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1050887736,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUwODg3NzM2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"dbbdf9","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1050888122,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUwODg4MTIy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/complexity%20%E2%86%92%20simple","name":"complexity → simple","color":"f99db1","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1050888509,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUwODg4NTA5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/api","name":"api","color":"522f99","default":false,"description":"Issues that require some work on the API (https://github.com/opencollective/opencollective-api)"},{"id":1050888694,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUwODg4Njk0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"b6adea","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1160115540,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTYwMTE1NTQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/stale","name":"stale","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":null},{"id":1404610126,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDA0NjEwMTI2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/rest","name":"rest","color":"d5a8ea","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1425169620,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDI1MTY5NjIw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/host%20dashboard","name":"host dashboard","color":"8bed68","default":false,"description":""},{"id":3370409719,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMzcwNDA5NzE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/labels/ocf","name":"ocf","color":"952E2D","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2020-01-13T21:28:10Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T13:14:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":1724461,"node_id":"IT_kwDOAMyFyc4AGlAt","name":"Enhancement","description":"An improvement or new functionality","color":"green","created_at":"2024-01-25T14:30:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T12:24:16Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"As a host admin, I want to be able to export data about my host (similar to the data export feature we offer Collectives), so that I can effectively own my data and use it for communication, administration, etc.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencollective/opencollective/issues/2808/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398","id":2535442316,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh86XH8eM","number":398,"title":"Vertex mapping for all functions that return a subgraph","user":{"login":"gdalle","id":22795598,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk1NTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22795598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle","html_url":"https://github.com/gdalle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdalle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3440932198,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh87NGHVm","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-19T06:46:32Z","updated_at":"2024-09-19T16:56:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> [!WARNING]\r\n> This is still a draft, the bounty has no legal value yet.\r\n\r\nAs recently pointed out on [Discourse](https://discourse.julialang.org/t/persistent-vertex-identities-for-steiner-tree-vertex-removal/119568/), some functions such as [`steiner_stree`](https://juliagraphs.org/Graphs.jl/stable/algorithms/steinertree/#Graphs.steiner_tree) return a subgraph without remembering which vertices from the original graph were selected. The original graph might have had vertices `1:N` and the subgraph `1:n`, but no mapping `1:n -> 1:N` is provided.\r\nThis contrasts with functions like [`induced_subgraph`](https://juliagraphs.org/Graphs.jl/stable/core_functions/operators/#Graphs.induced_subgraph-Union%7BTuple%7BT%7D,%20Tuple%7BU%7D,%20Tuple%7BT,%20AbstractVector%7BU%7D%7D%7D%20where%20%7BU%3C:Integer,%20T%3C:AbstractGraph%7D) which do return this mapping.\r\nIt would be nice to write down an exhaustive list of every subgraph-returning function in Graphs.jl, and make sure that each of them has a method/alternative that allows mapping back into the original graph.\r\n\r\nThe bounty completion requires API implementation, documentation (potentially also including good `See also` entries and a dedicated page), and testing.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Some familiarity with the average julia package-dev process.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: @gdalle or members of the JuliaGraphs community\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 1 month (except potential review overhead)\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure (for this particular bounty program):\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/398/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7","id":1144643798,"node_id":"I_kwDOG2iBZ85EOeDW","number":7,"title":"Funding Stan features","user":{"login":"spinkney","id":23704057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNzA0MDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23704057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney","html_url":"https://github.com/spinkney","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinkney/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2022-02-19T10:15:05Z","updated_at":"2022-03-02T20:27:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"An issue arose where a user offered to pay for a bounty to help get the feature included in Stan. We do not have a procedure for paying for features. This topic is to discuss how Stan should handle these requests and to make a public document on how a corporation or person can pay for feature development.\r\n\r\nA few non-exhaustive options:\r\n\r\n* Github bounties. This would require tracking bounties, typically by adding a 3rd party integration into Github such as https://issuehunt.io/. The benefit is that we may get more developers willing to work on the issue, the drawback is that the quality of the PR may come in to question resulting in a dispute over whether the contributor should be given the bounty. \r\n* Paying directly to Stan for the feature. We would have a track which estimates the development cost and then pays a _known_ Stan developer for their time. I have many questions on this route, like how does the estimation work? What if the feature is much more complex than originally thought? What happens if the feature does not make it in? I think many of these issues can be solved by explicit language in a work contract. Can we talk to Numfocus lawyers about getting a standard work-order for open-source software development?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stan-dev/sgb/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546/events","html_url":"https://github.com/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546","id":638853220,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2Mzg4NTMyMjA=","number":546,"title":"Exploring Project Sponsorship","user":{"login":"michaeljones","id":5390,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5390?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones","html_url":"https://github.com/michaeljones","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljones/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2020-06-15T13:26:51Z","updated_at":"2022-01-21T13:30:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm between jobs at the moment and looking to work primarily on freelance and contract work in the future. This mindset combined with watching the steady stream of activity and effort required to keep this project ticking along has led me to wonder if we should be exploring project sponsorship at all. \r\n\r\nI'm honestly not sure how to go about it but I'm curious if perhaps commercial companies are relying on Breathe to ship documentation for their products and if there is perhaps room to request support.\r\n\r\nI realise I have not been active for a long time and I wouldn't want to try to step in a start attempting to monetise this project when there has been significant work from many others. Any support to the project should be split fairly and primarily to those actively maintaining it. \r\n\r\nDoes anyone have any thoughts or experience on this? Do any of the users work at companies that could reasonably sponsor development in some form or other? ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/breathe-doc/breathe/issues/546/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714","id":849919175,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU4NDk5MTkxNzU=","number":714,"title":"Question: Support from NUMFOCUS","user":{"login":"noce2","id":20339399,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzM5Mzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20339399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2","html_url":"https://github.com/noce2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noce2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2021-04-04T17:14:40Z","updated_at":"2021-04-13T14:07:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- If you have a question, please first make sure it is not already answered in the README.md or https://cadquery.readthedocs.io -->\r\n\r\nHey all,\r\n\r\nHas anyone considered submitting the CadQuery project to [NumFOCUS' Fiscal Sponsorship Program](https://numfocus.org/projects-overview)?\r\n\r\nFor those unaware NumFOCUS is the organisation that ensures projects like Jupyter (the Notebook creators), Matplotlib, Pandas and others are well supported for the long term. I just started using CadQuery and have been really impressed with it so far and would love to see it continue to grow. NumFOCUS is itself sponsored by organisations like Microsoft, Amazon, IBM, Facebook and other industry heavyweights. A project accepted into NumFOCUS' project benefits from visibility, community and financial support. Keen to hear some thoughts.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CadQuery/cadquery/issues/714/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}